course: dictionary
lesson: 3068
title: Churches working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A big word can hide a simple idea. Ecumenism is a noun, a naming word for an idea. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Ecumenism means churches working together and seeking unity, for example in shared services and charities.» Working together and unity are the clues. Unity means being joined as one.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The spirit of ecumenism grew in the town.» Put in "the spirit of churches working together" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Ecumenical is the describing word, as in «ecumenical service».
explain: Ecumenism has a wider meaning too: friendship and cooperation between different religions or groups. The same clues help you here. Working together, friendship and sharing all point to people who are different but still joined in a common purpose.
fact: Ecumenism means the effort to bring different Christian churches together, so they understand each other, pray together and work together.
fact: An «ecumenical service» is a service shared by different churches.
fact: The Week of Prayer for Christian Unity is an ecumenical event.
fact: In a wider sense, ecumenism means friendship and cooperation between different religions or groups.
fact: Catholic, Protestant and Orthodox Christians may hold a shared service or work together on charity because of ecumenism.
exercise: What does ecumenism mean in the church sense? | A race between churches to build the tallest tower | A single church with only one priest | *Different churches coming together to understand each other, pray and work together
exercise: What is an «ecumenical service»? | A service with no songs or prayers | A service held by one church alone | *A service shared by different churches
exercise: «Ecumenism means churches working together and seeking unity.» Which word means unity? | Argument | Distance | *Togetherness | Silence
test: What is the wider meaning of ecumenism? | Keeping churches apart | *Friendship and cooperation between different religions or groups | Winning arguments between religions | Ignoring other religions
test: What is the Week of Prayer for Christian Unity? | *An ecumenical event where churches pray and work together for unity | A shopping festival | A music contest for schools
exam: Which sentence uses ecumenism correctly? | *Our town's churches held a shared service in the spirit of ecumenism | The shop sold ecumenism by the bag | Ecumenism is the name of the loudest bell in the church tower | The school choir practised ecumenism every Tuesday
